            lore: "<p>Modern archaeology has proven that the Icelandic sagas were not just legends. The Viking footprint has been found far beyond Europe.</p><p><strong>L'Anse aux Meadows (Newfoundland, Canada):</strong> The irrefutable proof that the Vikings reached North America 500 years before Christopher Columbus. In 1960, archaeologists discovered the foundations of eight peat buildings, ship rivets, and a spindle whorl (a weight for spinning wool), proving the presence of women on the expedition.</p>\n\n<h4 class=\"codex-section-title\"><i class=\"fas fa-gem\"></i> Other Major Archaeological Proofs</h4>\n<ul>\n    <li><strong>Runestones:</strong> Thousands are found, mainly in Sweden. These heavy standing stones commemorate journeys, those who died in battle, and alliances. The Jelling stone (Denmark) is even considered the \"birth certificate of Denmark\".</li>\n    <li><strong>Immense buried treasures:</strong> The Vikings brought back wealth from all over the world. The Spillings Hoard, discovered on the Swedish island of Gotland in 1999, contained over 14,000 pure silver Islamic coins, proving the power of their trade network all the way to the Middle East.</li>\n</ul>",
